msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid "We just released Quarkus 2.9, which comes packed with new features:"
msgstr ""

msgid "WebAuthn extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "Compression support for Reactive Routes and RESTEasy Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Confluent Schema Registry"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Back channel logout"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kotlin and Scala upgrade"
msgstr ""

msgid "And much more..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.8, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.9[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://webauthn.guide/[WebAuthn] is an authentication mechanism designed to "
"replace passwords. In short, every\n"
"time you write a service for registering new users, or logging them in, "
"instead of asking for a password, you\n"
"use WebAuthn, which will replace the password."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"WebAuthn replaces the password with a proof of identity. In practice, users, "
"instead of having to invent a password,\n"
"store it or remember it, will use a hardware token that will generate a "
"proof of identity specifically for your\n"
"service or website. This can be done by asking users to press their thumb on "
"their phone, or pressing a button\n"
"on a https://www.yubico.com[YubiKey] on a computer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Thanks to the new `quarkus-security-webauthn` extension,\n"
"you can implement WebAuthn authentication in your Quarkus applications."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find all the details about it in link:/guides/security-webauthn[the "
"dedicated guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenID Connect Providers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Well-known OIDC providers, such as GitHub, Google, Microsoft, Apple... are "
"very widely used to authenticate users in modern applications."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configuring them can be hard and require work for each of them to properly "
"understand how they implemented OIDC."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That's why Quarkus now comes with predefined settings for a lot of well-"
"known providers\n"
"and link:/guides/security-openid-connect-providers[an extensive "
"documentation] will guide you through setting things up."
msgstr ""

msgid "Providers currently covered are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "GitHub"
msgstr ""

msgid "Google"
msgstr ""

msgid "Microsoft"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apple"
msgstr ""

msgid "Facebook"
msgstr ""

msgid "Twitter"
msgstr ""

msgid "Spotify"
msgstr ""

msgid "More to come and contributions are very welcome in this area."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Quarkus 2.9, compression support has been added to Reactive Routes and "
"RESTEasy Reactive.\n"
"Body of HTTP responses can now be compressed with both these components."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More information in the link:/guides/reactive-routes#http-"
"compression[Reactive Routes guide]\n"
"and the link:/guides/resteasy-reactive#http-compression[RESTEasy Reactive "
"guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kafka - Add support for Confluent Schema Registry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We added support for the Confluent Schema Registry and restructured the "
"schema registry extensions for more flexibility."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The updated link:/guides/kafka-schema-registry-avro[Using Apache Kafka with "
"schema registry and Avro guide] contains everything you need to know about "
"these changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Back channel logout"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:/guides/security-openid-connect-web-authentication#back-channel-"
"logout[Support for OIDC backchannel logout] has been added."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add HTTP headers for specific paths"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Until now, you could configure additional HTTP headers globally.\n"
"But more often than not, you need to configure HTTP headers for a specific "
"subpath of your application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Starting with 2.9, you can use the new `quarkus.http.filter` configuration "
"properties to do so\n"
"as documented in the link:/guides/http-reference#additional-http-headers-per-"
"path[HTTP Reference guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Log rotation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.log.file.rotation.max-file-size` is now set to 10 MB by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "H2 2.1"
msgstr ""

msgid "We upgraded H2 to from 1.4 to 2.1."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This upgrade comes with a lot of changes, including some breaking ones.\n"
"The most common problems come from new reserved keywords such as `user`, "
"`value` or `timestamp`.\n"
"If you are using some of these keywords in your model, you will have to "
"adjust,\n"
"or switch to a container approach for testing instead of using H2."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kotlin 1.6.20"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kotlin has been upgraded to 1.6.20."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scala 2.13"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We upgraded to Scala 2.13.\n"
"Note that there is a https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-scala3[Scala 3 "
"extension in the Quarkiverse]."
msgstr ""

